From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Braumann <ripetitor@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 22 Sep 2026 01:30:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: ov5647: declare Rockchip camera module
 properties

The vendor OV5647 driver reads rockchip,camera-module-index, -facing,
-name and -lens-name and fails to probe with -EINVAL when any of them is
missing, but the binding sets additionalProperties: false and does not
declare them, so the Rockchip BSP device trees using this sensor (for
example the ELTAY RM66 reference carrier) do not validate against the
schema.

Document the four properties. They stay optional: mainline device trees
for the sensor do not provide them.

Signed-off-by: Sergey Braumann <ripetitor@proton.me>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/ovti,ov5647.yaml | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/ovti,ov5647.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/ovti,ov5647.yaml
@@ -30,6 +30,23 @@ properties:
     description: Reference to the GPIO connected to the pwdn pin. Active high.
     maxItems: 1
 
+  rockchip,camera-module-index:
+    description: Index of the camera module on the board.
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+
+  rockchip,camera-module-facing:
+    description: Facing of the camera module.
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string
+    enum: [back, front]
+
+  rockchip,camera-module-name:
+    description: Name of the camera module.
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string
+
+  rockchip,camera-module-lens-name:
+    description: Name of the camera module lens.
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string
+
   port:
     $ref: /schemas/graph.yaml#/$defs/port-base
     additionalProperties: false
